  "body": "A Windows 11 user reported that v0.23.0 \"kept crashing\" and uninstalled it. We had nothing to go on: no log, no GPU, no step.\n\nA check on a second Windows 11 machine (Intel Arc 140T + NVIDIA RTX 5050 laptop, v0.23.0 zip) found the app runs there with the default, dx12 and vulkan backends, so the crash is likely tied to the user's GPU/driver. It also found:\n\n- The adapter/backend line (\"gpu: using/adapter ...\") is printed to **stdout only**. It is not in the log file. A user who launches from the Start menu and sends us their log cannot tell us which GPU path crashed.\n\nWanted (smallest useful set):\n1. The chosen adapter (name, vendor, driver, backend) and the list of adapters found are written to the log file at startup.\n2. A panic, or a wgpu device/surface error at startup, is written to the log file with its message and a backtrace, before the process exits.\n3. The log file's location is easy to find (e.g. named in the About/Help dialog, or printed in the crash message).\n4. If startup fails on one backend, the error says which `--gpu-backend` values to try.\n\nDone means: launching on Windows without a terminal leaves a log file that names the adapter and backend, and a forced startup failure (e.g. `--gpu-backend` set to a backend the machine lacks) leaves its error in that log. Pinned by a test of the log setup where it can be tested headlessly.\n",
